---
// Literal recreation of the Claude Design canvas's Super Admin Dashboard
// screen (project/SuperAdmin.dc.html / SuperAdminDark.dc.html) — this
// REPLACES the earlier minimal placeholder that used to live at this same
// route (/super, unchanged). Shell: NavSidebar role="super" (its "super"
// role config in project/NavSidebar.dc.html, now updated with this turn's
// real "Overview"/"Access"/"System" grouping — see that file's own header
// comment) + a new dedicated SuperNavTop.astro (the artboard bakes its own
// header markup directly, same as Admin.dc.html did, so it gets its own
// component rather than reusing the generic NavTop.astro — see that
// component's own header comment for the full reasoning).
//
// PERMISSIONS: unchanged — /super is already gated to super_admin only by
// src/middleware.ts (ROLE_GATED_PREFIXES, from lib/roles.ts), not touched
// this turn. No RLS, no migration, no schema change anywhere in this turn —
// every real value below is read through RLS policies that already exist
// and already grant super_admin unscoped access (profiles_select_all_for_admin,
// orders_select_staff, approval_requests_select_super_admin,
// audit_logs_select_super_admin — all confirmed live before writing this
// page, not assumed).
//
// NO-FABRICATION DECISIONS — every KPI/chart/table value below is real,
// computed from existing tables/RPCs already used elsewhere in this project
// (profiles, orders via dashboard_revenue_trend, approval_requests,
// audit_logs — zero new RPCs/views/migrations). Where the design shows a
// number/concept this schema genuinely has no equivalent for, it is either
// honestly omitted or relabeled to what it actually is — never copied from
// the demo, never silently reinterpreted:
//  - "Revenue · year to date" / "▲ 12.4% vs last year" / sparkline: real
//    calendar-YTD revenue (dashboard_revenue_trend RPC, same real function
//    every other dashboard uses — excludes cancelled orders). The
//    year-over-year %% is real when the same calendar-YTD window last year
//    had any revenue to compare against; this project's live data only
//    starts in September 2026, so an honest "No orders last year" is shown
//    instead of a fabricated percentage. The sparkline reuses the same 6
//    real monthly points as the "Revenue by month" panel below (only
//    rendered once ≥2 real months have data).
//  - "Customer accounts" / "+38 new this month": real count of profiles
//    with role='customer', real count of those with created_at in the
//    current real IST calendar month. "No new customers this month" shown
//    honestly when that count is zero.
//  - "Active users" / "46" / "Internal team · +3 this month": real count of
//    every non-customer profile (sales_staff/inventory_staff/admin/
//    super_admin), real count of those created this month.
//  - "Uptime · 30 days" / "99.98%" / the day-by-day uptime bar: DROPPED
//    entirely, not even as a disabled placeholder. No server/infrastructure
//    health monitoring exists anywhere in this project — this is exactly
//    the "uptime percentage"/"system metric" the no-fabrication rules
//    explicitly forbid inventing, and there is no honest partial version of
//    it to show. Replaced with a genuinely real 4th KPI instead: "Pending
//    approvals" (approval_requests where status='pending') — real count,
//    thematically the correct kind of thing for a Super Admin to see at a
//    glance (the same table review_approval_request() operates on), not
//    invented to fill the grid slot.
//  - Header "All systems normal" status pill: dropped entirely, same reason
//    as the uptime KPI above — no real system-health signal exists.
//  - Header "Invite user" button: omitted — see SuperNavTop.astro's own
//    header comment (a real inviteStaff action exists, but its real UI
//    lives on /admin/staff, not here, and this turn only rebuilds the
//    Dashboard).
//  - "Revenue by month": real IST calendar-month revenue for the trailing 6
//    real months (dashboard_revenue_trend RPC, bucketed by month here
//    exactly like /admin's own "Revenue trend" chart already does), shown
//    as the design's own horizontal bar-row layout with real ₹ amounts —
//    not the demo's fabricated 28/31/33/32/35.8/38.6 figures.
//  - "Team accounts by role": real profiles grouped by role, restricted to
//    the 4 real staff roles (customer excluded — this panel is about the
//    internal team, matching the design's own "N active internal users"
//    framing). Real total, real per-role counts and real donut proportions
//    — not the demo's fabricated 22/18/4/2. "Manage roles & permissions →"
//    link omitted: /super/roles doesn't exist yet (explicitly out of scope
//    this turn) and linking to a route that doesn't exist would be worse
//    than no link (same reasoning /admin's own dashboard already used for
//    its own not-yet-built destinations).
//  - "Recent user activity": relabeled from the demo's fake roster to the 5
//    real most-recently-created non-customer profiles (name, role, and
//    "Joined" — real created_at — real Active/Inactive from the real
//    is_active column). The design's "Last sign-in" column has no real
//    equivalent anywhere in this schema (no sign-in tracking is exposed
//    beyond auth.users, which nothing in this app currently reads) —
//    relabeled to "Joined" rather than fabricated. The design's "Invited"
//    status also has no real equivalent (is_active is a real two-state
//    boolean, not a three-state lifecycle) — only real Active/Inactive ever
//    render. "All users" link omitted: /super/users doesn't exist yet.
//  - "Audit log": real audit_logs rows (already unscoped-readable by
//    super_admin via audit_logs_select_super_admin), real actor name (join
//    profiles), real timestamp. Rendered into a real sentence per real
//    `action` value this schema actually produces today (staff_invited,
//    approval_approved, approval_rejected — the only three actions any code
//    in this project ever inserts), with approval_approved/rejected further
//    enriched with the real target action_type via a join to
//    approval_requests when approval_request_id is set. Any future action
//    value this schema doesn't know how to phrase yet falls back to a
//    plain, still-entirely-real "{actor} — {action} on {entity_table}"
//    rather than being hidden or invented. "Open log" link omitted:
//    /super/audit-log doesn't exist yet.
//  - Header "Export" button: no export/report-generation capability exists
//    anywhere in this project — omitted (same precedent as /admin's own
//    dashboard).
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavSidebar from "../../components/staff/NavSidebar.astro";
import SuperNavTop from "../../components/staff/SuperNavTop.astro";
import { resolveDashboardRange } from "../../lib/dashboardRange";

// dashboard_revenue_trend's real return shape (day/revenue/order_count) —
// not present in the generated Supabase types (RPC return rows come back
// untyped), so annotated explicitly here, same as /admin's own dashboard.
interface RevenueTrendRow {
  day: string;
  revenue: number;
  order_count: number;
}

interface ProfileRow {
  id: string;
  role: "customer" | "sales_staff" | "inventory_staff" | "admin" | "super_admin";
  full_name: string | null;
  is_active: boolean;
  created_at: string;
}

interface AuditLogRow {
  id: string;
  actor_id: string;
  action: string;
  entity_table: string;
  entity_id: string;
  new_value: Record<string, unknown> | null;
  approval_request_id: string | null;
  created_at: string;
}

const ROLE_LABEL: Record<ProfileRow["role"], string> = {
  customer: "Customer",
  sales_staff: "Sales staff",
  inventory_staff: "Inventory staff",
  admin: "Admin",
  super_admin: "Super admin",
};

const ACTION_TYPE_LABEL: Record<string, string> = {
  delete_product: "a delete-product",
  deactivate_staff: "a deactivate-staff",
  change_role: "a change-role",
  cancel_paid_order: "a cancel-order",
  refund_payment: "a refund-payment",
};

// Same IST-anchoring technique dashboardRange.ts already uses, generalized
// to calendar-month boundaries (needed here because dashboardRange.ts only
// exports fixed day-count/YTD presets, not month boundaries) — identical
// helper to the one /admin/index.astro already defines for itself.
const IST_OFFSET_MS = 5.5 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
function istMonthBoundsUtc(year: number, month0: number): { from: string; to: string } {
  const fromUtcMs = Date.UTC(year, month0, 1) - IST_OFFSET_MS;
  const toUtcMs = Date.UTC(year, month0 + 1, 1) - IST_OFFSET_MS;
  return { from: new Date(fromUtcMs).toISOString(), to: new Date(toUtcMs).toISOString() };
}
const nowIst = new Date(Date.now() + IST_OFFSET_MS);
const curYear = nowIst.getUTCFullYear();
const curMonth0 = nowIst.getUTCMonth();
const thisMonth = istMonthBoundsUtc(curYear, curMonth0);
const MONTH_LABELS = ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr", "May", "Jun", "Jul", "Aug", "Sep", "Oct", "Nov", "Dec"];

const ytd = resolveDashboardRange("ytd");
// Same calendar-YTD window, one year earlier, for an apples-to-apples
// year-over-year comparison (Jan 1 last year through "today" last year).
const lastYearYtd = istMonthBoundsUtc(curYear - 1, 0);
lastYearYtd.to = new Date(Date.UTC(curYear - 1, curMonth0, nowIst.getUTCDate() + 1) - IST_OFFSET_MS).toISOString();
const sixMoStart = istMonthBoundsUtc(curYear, curMonth0 - 5).from;

const [
  { data: profileRows },
  { data: ytdRevenueRows },
  { data: lastYearRevenueRows },
  { data: sixMoRevenueRows },
  { count: pendingApprovalCount },
  { data: auditRows },
] = await Promise.all([
  Astro.locals.supabase.from("profiles").select("id, role, full_name, is_active, created_at"),
  Astro.locals.supabase.rpc("dashboard_revenue_trend", { p_from: ytd.from, p_to: ytd.to }),
  Astro.locals.supabase.rpc("dashboard_revenue_trend", { p_from: lastYearYtd.from, p_to: lastYearYtd.to }),
  Astro.locals.supabase.rpc("dashboard_revenue_trend", { p_from: sixMoStart, p_to: thisMonth.to }),
  Astro.locals.supabase.from("approval_requests").select("id", { count: "exact", head: true }).eq("status", "pending"),
  Astro.locals.supabase
    .from("audit_logs")
    .select("id, actor_id, action, entity_table, entity_id, new_value, approval_request_id, created_at")
    .order("created_at", { ascending: false })
    .limit(5),
]);

const formatCurrency = (value: number) =>
  new Intl.NumberFormat("en-IN", { style: "currency", currency: "INR", maximumFractionDigits: 0 }).format(value);

const profiles = (profileRows ?? []) as ProfileRow[];
const STAFF_ROLES = ["inventory_staff", "sales_staff", "admin", "super_admin"] as const;

// --- Customer accounts ---
const customers = profiles.filter((p) => p.role === "customer");
const newCustomersThisMonth = customers.filter((p) => p.created_at >= thisMonth.from).length;

// --- Active users (internal team) ---
const staff = profiles.filter((p) => p.role !== "customer");
const newStaffThisMonth = staff.filter((p) => p.created_at >= thisMonth.from).length;

// --- Revenue · YTD, real vs. last year ---
const sumRevenue = (rows: RevenueTrendRow[] | null) => (rows ?? []).reduce((sum, r) => sum + Number(r.revenue), 0);
const ytdRevenue = sumRevenue(ytdRevenueRows as RevenueTrendRow[] | null);
const lastYearRevenue = sumRevenue(lastYearRevenueRows as RevenueTrendRow[] | null);
const yoyChangePct = lastYearRevenue > 0 ? ((ytdRevenue - lastYearRevenue) / lastYearRevenue) * 100 : null;

// --- Revenue by month, trailing 6 real IST calendar months (zero-filled —
// a real zero for a month with genuinely no orders, not an invented one) ---
const revenueByMonth = new Map<string, number>();
for (const r of (sixMoRevenueRows ?? []) as RevenueTrendRow[]) {
  const ym = String(r.day).slice(0, 7);
  revenueByMonth.set(ym, (revenueByMonth.get(ym) ?? 0) + Number(r.revenue));
}
const monthBars = Array.from({ length: 6 }, (_, i) => {
  const d = new Date(Date.UTC(curYear, curMonth0 - 5 + i, 1));
  const ym = `${d.getUTCFullYear()}-${String(d.getUTCMonth() + 1).padStart(2, "0")}`;
  return { label: MONTH_LABELS[d.getUTCMonth()], value: revenueByMonth.get(ym) ?? 0 };
});
const monthBarsMax = Math.max(...monthBars.map((m) => m.value), 1);

// Revenue KPI sparkline reuses these same 6 real monthly points.
const sparkPoints = monthBars.map((m) => m.value);
const sparkMax = Math.max(...sparkPoints, 1);
const sparkSvgPoints = sparkPoints
  .map((v, i) => {
    const x = (i / (sparkPoints.length - 1)) * 96;
    const y = 34 - (v / sparkMax) * 32;
    return `${x.toFixed(1)},${y.toFixed(1)}`;
  })
  .join(" ");
const hasRealSparkline = sparkPoints.some((v) => v > 0) && sparkPoints.length > 1;

// --- Team accounts by role (donut) ---
const roleCounts = new Map<string, number>();
for (const r of STAFF_ROLES) roleCounts.set(r, staff.filter((p) => p.role === r).length);
const totalStaff = staff.length;
const ROLE_COLOR: Record<string, string> = {
  inventory_staff: "var(--sd-accent)",
  sales_staff: "var(--sd-chart2)",
  admin: "var(--sd-fg)",
  super_admin: "var(--sd-input)",
};
const CIRCUMFERENCE = 2 * Math.PI * 60;
let cumulative = 0;
const donutSegments = STAFF_ROLES.map((r) => {
  const count = roleCounts.get(r) ?? 0;
  const frac = totalStaff > 0 ? count / totalStaff : 0;
  const len = frac * CIRCUMFERENCE;
  const seg = {
    role: r,
    label: ROLE_LABEL[r],
    count,
    color: ROLE_COLOR[r],
    dasharray: `${len.toFixed(2)} ${(CIRCUMFERENCE - len).toFixed(2)}`,
    dashoffset: (-cumulative).toFixed(2),
  };
  cumulative += len;
  return seg;
});

// --- Recent user activity: 5 most-recently-created real internal-team
// profiles (customers excluded — this panel mirrors the design's own
// "internal team" framing, same scope as the Active users KPI above) ---
const recentActivity = [...staff].sort((a, b) => (a.created_at < b.created_at ? 1 : -1)).slice(0, 5);

// --- Audit log: real rows, enriched with real actor names + (when set) the
// real approval_requests.action_type behind an approval_approved/rejected
// entry ---
const audit = (auditRows ?? []) as AuditLogRow[];
const actorIds = [...new Set(audit.map((a) => a.actor_id))];
const actorNameById = new Map<string, string>();
for (const id of actorIds) {
  const known = profiles.find((p) => p.id === id);
  if (known) actorNameById.set(id, known.full_name || "—");
}
const missingActorIds = actorIds.filter((id) => !actorNameById.has(id));
if (missingActorIds.length > 0) {
  const { data: extraProfiles } = await Astro.locals.supabase.from("profiles").select("id, full_name").in("id", missingActorIds);
  for (const p of extraProfiles ?? []) actorNameById.set(p.id as string, (p.full_name as string) || "—");
}

const approvalIds = [...new Set(audit.map((a) => a.approval_request_id).filter((id): id is string => !!id))];
const actionTypeByApprovalId = new Map<string, string>();
if (approvalIds.length > 0) {
  const { data: approvalRows } = await Astro.locals.supabase.from("approval_requests").select("id, action_type").in("id", approvalIds);
  for (const r of approvalRows ?? []) actionTypeByApprovalId.set(r.id as string, r.action_type as string);
}

function auditLineFor(entry: AuditLogRow): { text: string; dotColor: string } {
  const actorName = actorNameById.get(entry.actor_id) ?? "—";
  if (entry.action === "staff_invited") {
    const email = (entry.new_value?.email as string | undefined) ?? "a new user";
    const role = entry.new_value?.role as ProfileRow["role"] | undefined;
    return { text: `${actorName} invited ${email} as ${role ? ROLE_LABEL[role] : "staff"}`, dotColor: "var(--sd-accent)" };
  }
  if (entry.action === "approval_approved" || entry.action === "approval_rejected") {
    const actionType = entry.approval_request_id ? actionTypeByApprovalId.get(entry.approval_request_id) : undefined;
    const actionLabel = actionType ? ACTION_TYPE_LABEL[actionType] ?? `a ${actionType}` : "an approval";
    const verb = entry.action === "approval_approved" ? "approved" : "rejected";
    return {
      text: `${actorName} ${verb} ${actionLabel} request`,
      dotColor: entry.action === "approval_approved" ? "var(--sd-success-fg)" : "var(--sd-danger-fg)",
    };
  }
  return { text: `${actorName} — ${entry.action} on ${entry.entity_table}`, dotColor: "var(--sd-muted-fg)" };
}
const auditEntries = audit.map((a) => ({
  ...auditLineFor(a),
  meta: new Date(a.created_at).toLocaleString("en-IN", {
    day: "numeric",
    month: "short",
    hour: "2-digit",
    minute: "2-digit",
    timeZone: "Asia/Kolkata",
  }),
}));

const todayLabel = new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-IN", { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric", timeZone: "Asia/Kolkata" });
---

<BaseLayout title="Platform overview — Super Admin">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="sd" id="sd-root">
    <div id="sd-sidebar-backdrop" class="sd__backdrop"></div>

    <div id="sd-sidebar" class="sd__sidebar">
      <NavSidebar active="Overview" role="super" />
    </div>

    <div class="sd__panel">
      <SuperNavTop section="Dashboard" page="Overview" />

      <main id="main-content" class="sa__main">
        <div class="sa__header">
          <div class="sa__heading-col">
            <h1>Platform overview</h1>
            <span class="sa__subtitle">Store-wide · as of {todayLabel}</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sa__kpis">
          <div class="sa__kpi-card">
            <span class="sa__kpi-label">Revenue · year to date</span>
            <div class="sa__kpi-row">
              <div class="sa__kpi-col">
                <span class="sa__kpi-value">{formatCurrency(ytdRevenue)}</span>
                <span class="sa__kpi-note">
                  {yoyChangePct !== null ? (
                    <Fragment>
                      <span class={yoyChangePct >= 0 ? "sa__delta-up" : "sa__delta-down"}>
                        {yoyChangePct >= 0 ? "▲" : "▼"} {Math.abs(yoyChangePct).toFixed(1)}%
                      </span>{" "}
                      vs last year
                    </Fragment>
                  ) : (
                    "No orders last year"
                  )}
                </span>
              </div>
              {hasRealSparkline && (
                <svg width="96" height="36" viewBox="0 0 96 36" aria-hidden="true" class="sa__sparkline">
                  <polyline points={sparkSvgPoints} fill="none" stroke="var(--sd-accent)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
                </svg>
              )}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sa__kpi-card">
            <span class="sa__kpi-label">Customer accounts</span>
            <div class="sa__kpi-col">
              <span class="sa__kpi-value">{customers.length}</span>
              <span class="sa__kpi-note">
                {newCustomersThisMonth > 0 ? (
                  <Fragment><span class="sa__delta-up">+{newCustomersThisMonth}</span> new this month</Fragment>
                ) : (
                  "No new customers this month"
                )}
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sa__kpi-card">
            <span class="sa__kpi-label">Active users</span>
            <div class="sa__kpi-col">
              <span class="sa__kpi-value">{staff.length}</span>
              <span class="sa__kpi-note">
                Internal team ·{" "}
                {newStaffThisMonth > 0 ? (
                  <Fragment><span class="sa__delta-up">+{newStaffThisMonth}</span> this month</Fragment>
                ) : (
                  "no new members this month"
                )}
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sa__kpi-card">
            <div class="sa__kpi-top">
              <span class="sa__kpi-label">Pending approvals</span>
              {(pendingApprovalCount ?? 0) > 0 && <span class="sa__needs-action">Needs review</span>}
            </div>
            <div class="sa__kpi-col">
              <span class="sa__kpi-value">{pendingApprovalCount ?? 0}</span>
              <span class="sa__kpi-note">Awaiting super admin review</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sa__charts">
          <section class="sa__chart-card">
            <div class="sa__section-head">
              <div class="sa__section-head-col">
                <h2>Revenue by month</h2>
                <span class="sa__section-sub">Last 6 months · real orders, cancelled excluded</span>
              </div>
              <span class="sa__legend">Total {formatCurrency(monthBars.reduce((s, m) => s + m.value, 0))}</span>
            </div>
            <div
              role="img"
              aria-label={`Monthly revenue: ${monthBars.map((m) => `${m.label} ${formatCurrency(m.value)}`).join(", ")}`}
              class="sa__month-bars"
            >
              {monthBars.map((b) => (
                <div class="sa__month-row">
                  <span class="sa__month-label">{b.label}</span>
                  <div class="sa__month-track"><div class="sa__month-fill" style={`width:${(b.value / monthBarsMax) * 100}%`}></div></div>
                  <span class="sa__month-value">{formatCurrency(b.value)}</span>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="sa__side-card">
            <div class="sa__section-head-col">
              <h2>Team accounts by role</h2>
              <span class="sa__section-sub">{totalStaff} active internal user{totalStaff === 1 ? "" : "s"}</span>
            </div>
            {totalStaff > 0 ? (
              <div class="sa__donut-row">
                <svg width="150" height="150" viewBox="0 0 150 150" role="img" aria-label={donutSegments.map((s) => `${s.label} ${s.count}`).join(", ")}>
                  <g transform="rotate(-90 75 75)" fill="none" stroke-width="18">
                    {donutSegments.map((s) => (
                      <circle cx="75" cy="75" r="60" stroke={s.color} stroke-dasharray={s.dasharray} stroke-dashoffset={s.dashoffset} />
                    ))}
                  </g>
                  <text x="75" y="72" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Geist, sans-serif" font-size="24" font-weight="600" class="sa__donut-total">{totalStaff}</text>
                  <text x="75" y="92" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Geist, sans-serif" font-size="11" class="sa__donut-unit">users</text>
                </svg>
                <div class="sa__donut-legend">
                  {donutSegments.map((s) => (
                    <div class="sa__donut-legend-row">
                      <span class="sa__donut-swatch" style={`background:${s.color}`}></span>
                      <span class="sa__donut-legend-label">{s.label}</span>
                      <span class="sa__donut-legend-count">{s.count}</span>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </div>
            ) : (
              <p class="sa__empty">No internal team accounts yet.</p>
            )}
          </section>
        </div>

        <div class="sa__bottom">
          <section class="sa__activity-card">
            <div class="sa__section-head sa__section-head--padded">
              <h2>Recent user activity</h2>
            </div>
            {recentActivity.length > 0 ? (
              <Fragment>
                <div class="sa__activity-grid sa__activity-grid--head">
                  <span>User</span><span>Role</span><span>Joined</span><span>Status</span>
                </div>
                {recentActivity.map((p) => {
                  const initials =
                    (p.full_name || "—")
                      .split(/\s+/)
                      .filter(Boolean)
                      .slice(0, 2)
                      .map((part) => part[0]?.toUpperCase())
                      .join("") || "?";
                  return (
                    <div class="sa__activity-grid sa__activity-row">
                      <span class="sa__activity-user">
                        <span class="sa__activity-avatar">{initials}</span>
                        <span class="sa__activity-name">{p.full_name || "—"}</span>
                      </span>
                      <span><span class="sa__role-pill">{ROLE_LABEL[p.role]}</span></span>
                      <span class="sa__activity-joined">{new Date(p.created_at).toLocaleDateString("en-IN", { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric", timeZone: "Asia/Kolkata" })}</span>
                      <span><span class={`sa__status-pill ${p.is_active ? "sa__status-pill--active" : "sa__status-pill--inactive"}`}>{p.is_active ? "Active" : "Inactive"}</span></span>
                    </div>
                  );
                })}
              </Fragment>
            ) : (
              <p class="sa__empty">No internal team accounts yet.</p>
            )}
          </section>

          <section class="sa__audit-card">
            <div class="sa__section-head">
              <h2>Audit log</h2>
            </div>
            {auditEntries.length > 0 ? (
              <div class="sa__audit-list">
                {auditEntries.map((l) => (
                  <div class="sa__audit-row">
                    <span class="sa__audit-dot" style={`background:${l.dotColor}`}></span>
                    <div class="sa__audit-col">
                      <span class="sa__audit-text">{l.text}</span>
                      <span class="sa__audit-meta">{l.meta}</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            ) : (
              <p class="sa__empty">No audit activity yet.</p>
            )}
          </section>
        </div>
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

